# Internal authoring material: NOT for the public repo.
# context/ holds the full run-of-show and briefs for all 45 sessions;
# publishing it would leak every future class at once.
# tools/ is the private build machinery (manifest + site generator + release helper);
# it runs locally and only its output (index.html, README.md) is published.
context/
CLAUDE.md
tools/

# Unreleased classes: kept out of the repo until their teaching day.
# tools/release.py removes the matching line (and clears the manifest hold)
# when a class is published, so a stray `git add -A` can never leak future work.

